nnect state restructuring with religious transformation."}, {"id": "b60e476a-29cd-4376-8d28-d44c57f1766e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Migration, frontier, and political fragmentation", "children": [{"id": "d6c47036-ac25-4ca0-abfb-28212aa193f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Goths"}, {"id": "70884504-f740-44d4-9118-56c8ef3b3dc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Huns"}, {"id": "e3dec966-31d6-4bb6-8a0d-e215c295cf8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vandals"}, {"id": "4a8aefaa-e5b5-4c0a-bfa8-de753a289d6d", "type": "concept", "title": "federates"}, {"id": "c9a0fef4-8e9f-4719-a418-5c4ea515a9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "frontier diplomacy"}, {"id": "00e39732-1a39-42fd-8ac1-6ded6abbcb16", "type": "concept", "title": "Adrianople"}, {"id": "b23973f6-bce9-4b99-921c-cb7e189c5f2c", "type": "concept", "title": "sack of Rome"}, {"id": "4c346949-58c1-48e5-acfb-f7d7c79df257", "type": "concept", "title": "476 CE"}], "description": "This subtopic studies frontier peoples and Roman responses without treating them as simple invaders."}, {"id": "694604ed-487f-46b3-b40a-d477988daef4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuity, Byzantium, and new worlds", "children": [{"id": "be0c808e-0664-495a-9682-8c5ac2fa877e", "type": "concept", "title": "Byzantium"}, {"id": "bc030409-0241-4285-99fb-63b3325dbf36", "type": "concept", "title": "Justinian"}, {"id": "1c5dec84-6191-4e85-8319-5c51d353145b", "type": "concept", "title": "Codex Justinianus"}, {"id": "95c5b25f-9e10-4dc0-8959-43a1b22aa20c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ravenna"}, {"id": "fb381d90-1ad6-4670-835a-f90bac570d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediterranean trade"}, {"id": "95c3078d-2a4e-4c69-920a-47a43cb712d0", "type": "concept", "title": "urban change"}, {"id": "1499773b-f156-4a86-8637-9b6bcde0010d", "type": "concept", "title": "late antique culture"}, {"id": "d6706d00-a3f5-47ae-a9b7-c20c939928b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Islamic conquests as later transition"}], "description": "Students examine what changed and what continued after western imperial collapse."}]}, {"id": "5e73eaa9-5159-4882-b6d2-8c34f557ef6d", "type": "topic", "title": "Historiography, Archaeology, and Reception of the Ancient World", "description": "This topic asks how ancient history has been written, excavated, collected, displayed, and reused in later politics and culture. Students become critical readers of both ancient evidence and modern interpretations.", "children": [{"id": "a6cf5a90-4940-43d3-81f9-4b6c1c4a77be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ancient historians and genres", "children": [{"id": "98c2d4e7-12c5-4813-ba15-64d2536b8e95", "type": "concept", "title": "Herodotus"}, {"id": "6e0b3952-c47d-4a91-9b8c-8d201c69d136", "type": "concept", "title": "Thucydides"}, {"id": "7a46ce97-0bf7-4e6d-a2b9-a8b20d05f0ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Polybius"}, {"id": "60cc4779-e612-4f65-9fc9-5efb3fe2ead3", "type": "concept", "title": "Livy"}, {"id": "9f80adc8-e7f8-4525-b7d7-b06c36b31c4c", "type": "concept", "title": "Tacitus"}, {"id": "4f94c224-0d07-4d43-aa19-dea5aca1e7b1", "type": "concept", "title": "biography"}, {"id": "b5790610-9718-4db7-8359-53ac79542614", "type": "concept", "title": "annals"}, {"id": "c8ed3049-7e1e-45ac-b8dc-2904f4f0bd0f", "type": "concept", "title": "ethnography"}, {"id": "bae907fd-6fb8-42f3-969d-c4baacce677d", "type": "concept", "title": "rhetoric"}], "description": "Students learn how ancient authors shaped historical memory through genre and purpose."}, {"id": "37ac95c7-9bb0-476d-8851-d23672e7eaf6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Archaeology and material interpretation", "children": [{"id": "f2436815-c08a-4d8b-9efe-51e96d0c2b1e", "type": "concept", "title": "stratigraphy"}, {"id": "981a6900-592d-4aec-9e5b-b84f2f6c9c26", "type": "concept", "title": "typology"}, {"id": "816a5595-2a20-4bde-8276-cee4a1b9834d", "type": "concept", "title": "survey archaeology"}, {"id": "5b4f21f0-3a9d-4842-8cc1-66d2b1d29a53", "type": "concept", "title": "excavation"}, {"id": "24cb0a3e-9306-45d1-9461-942629ca2c03", "type": "