ents connect state restructuring with religious transformation."}, {"id": "b60e476a-29cd-4376-8d28-d44c57f1766e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Migration, frontier, and political fragmentation", "children": [{"id": "d6c47036-ac25-4ca0-abfb-28212aa193f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Goths"}, {"id": "70884504-f740-44d4-9118-56c8ef3b3dc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Huns"}, {"id": "e3dec966-31d6-4bb6-8a0d-e215c295cf8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vandals"}, {"id": "4a8aefaa-e5b5-4c0a-bfa8-de753a289d6d", "type": "concept", "title": "federates"}, {"id": "c9a0fef4-8e9f-4719-a418-5c4ea515a9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "frontier diplomacy"}, {"id": "00e39732-1a39-42fd-8ac1-6ded6abbcb16", "type": "concept", "title": "Adrianople"}, {"id": "b23973f6-bce9-4b99-921c-cb7e189c5f2c", "type": "concept", "title": "sack of Rome"}, {"id": "4c346949-58c1-48e5-acfb-f7d7c79df257", "type": "concept", "title": "476 CE"}], "description": "This subtopic studies frontier peoples and Roman responses without treating them as simple invaders."}, {"id": "694604ed-487f-46b3-b40a-d477988daef4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuity, Byzantium, and new worlds", "children": [{"id": "be0c808e-0664-495a-9682-8c5ac2fa877e", "type": "concept", "title": "Byzantium"}, {"id": "bc030409-0241-4285-99fb-63b3325dbf36", "type": "concept", "title": "Justinian"}, {"id": "1c5dec84-6191-4e85-8319-5c51d353145b", "type": "concept", "title": "Codex Justinianus"}, {"id": "95c5b25f-9e10-4dc0-8959-43a1b22aa20c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ravenna"}, {"id": "fb381d90-1ad6-4670-835a-f90bac570d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediterranean trade"}, {"id": "95c3078d-2a4e-4c69-920a-47a43cb712d0", "type": "concept", "title": "urban change"}, {"id": "1499773b-f156-4a86-8637-9b6bcde0010d", "type": "concept", "title": "late antique culture"}, {"id": "d6706d00-a3f5-47ae-a9b7-c20c939928b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Islamic conquests as later transition"}], "description": "Students examine what changed and what cont